  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We give a finite-boundary alternative proof of Mertens's grid–cylinder growth equality (2024, Section 5, page 19, after equation (22)), which already follows from Gangloff and Talon's grid results (2019/2020). The per-vertex counts have the same unrestricted joint limit as both side lengths tend to infinity. An injective boundary repair gives g(m,n) <= c(m,n) <= 4^n g(m,n). Block arguments yield explicit rectangle and strip bounds, and the comparison extends to every positive activity and to king graphs with periodic boundaries.",
